 "title": "Pediatric stridor decision chart: the phase of stridor localizes the narrowing; an infectious cause is croup (barking cough, steeple sign, the most common) or epiglottitis (drooling, tripod, secure the airway), and a choking episode points to foreign body aspiration (inspiratory and expiratory chest X-ray, rigid bronchoscopy if history, exam or imaging is positive)",
